%% Runtime — one booking run (section 6.1)
%% Diagrams as code. Render with any Mermaid renderer.
sequenceDiagram
    actor U as User
    participant D as Driver (separate project)
    participant A as Autobook commands
    participant PL as paperless-ngx
    participant S as Staging
    participant L as Ledger package
    participant F as Ledger files

    D->>D: get the statement, convert it to OFX (outside Autobook)
    D->>A: autobook propose FILE…
    A->>A: parse OFX, admit each statement whole or not at all
    A->>L: read coa, corpus, existing
    L->>F: load the main file and its includes
    L-->>A: contracts
    A->>A: normalise, dedup, correlate (transfers, match_existing)
    A->>PL: bill metadata for the batch window
    A->>A: link bills, classify, disposition, batch gate, version gate
    alt a statement is rejected at admission
        A-->>D: exit 7, reason per file, nothing staged from that statement
    else batch gate or version gate refuses
        A-->>D: exit 3, nothing written
    else rows to review
        A->>S: stage proposals
        A-->>D: exit 0
        D->>A: autobook review-file
        A-->>D: review file on standard output (gated rows pre-marked a)
        D->>U: open the review file in an editor
        U-->>D: saved = approval of rows marked a
        D->>A: autobook apply --from FILE
        A->>A: take the writer lock, recover any journal, check kept pre-images (a refusal is exit 4, staging unchanged)
        A->>A: strict parse by ID (a parse error is exit 5, nothing applied)
        A->>S: approve / correct / reject
        Note over D,L: until build step 5 the driver calls autobook decide instead. Decisions recorded, nothing written
        A->>L: apply-in with the approved rows
        L->>F: 1 read, SHA-256 of every file (owned file not included or root names differ is exit 4)
        L->>L: 2 filter, drop rows whose proposal ID is in the ledger and matched rows whose applied_entry is still present
        L->>L: 3 check each row (accounts open, currency, exact zero sum), a failing row is queued
        alt only matched rows
            L->>F: skip render, journal and exchange; load again, steps 6 and 7 against the fresh load
        else created rows
            L->>L: 4 render the entries
            L->>F: 5 compare all hashes and kept pre-images (a change is exit 4), write the journal, checked atomic exchange with the owned file
            L->>F: 6 read back, every created ID exactly once as approved, every matched entry still the only candidate
        end
        L->>L: 7 assert (no new load error, nothing else changed, balances moved by the postings written, kept pre-images unchanged)
        alt read-back or an assertion fails, created rows
            L->>F: exchange back to the previous content, keep the rejected batch as a pre-image
            L-->>A: nothing applied
            A-->>D: exit 6
        else a check fails, only matched rows
            L-->>A: nothing applied, nothing to restore
            A-->>D: exit 6
        else all pass
            L-->>A: apply-out with proposal_id, entry, status
            A->>S: mark rows applied, record applied_entry
            A-->>D: exit 0
        end
    end
    D->>U: notify (the driver's job)
